TzD (task #42): read adjacent header fields through the header pointer.
GRO reads two adjacent 16-bit fields as one 32-bit word through the
first field's address: *(u32 *)&th->source (source and dest ports),
*(__be32 *)&iph->id (id and frag_off).  TzD bounds &p->field to that
field, so the 4-byte read traps (inet_gro_receive).  Take the address
from the header instead, (u8 *)(p) + offsetof(typeof(*(p)), field): the
same bytes, bounded by the header.
